# Deployment-local PRIVATE workspace (disposable, never version controlled).
#
# `deployment/.test/` is where an agent or a test keeps throwaway material for THIS deployment:
# temporary fixtures, screenshots, generated reports, browser artifacts, probes, copied files.
# Nothing inside it is ever committed — not even a `.gitkeep` — so an agent that needs the
# directory creates it locally (see `deployment/AGENTS.md`).
.test/

# The deployment's own OPERATIONAL RECORD (FOUNDATION-B4A, written since B4B) — generated state, never
# authored content.
#
# `operational-state.json` is what this deployment is RUNNING and what has happened to it (the live
# Foundation release and deployment revision, the candidate in flight, the last failure, the rollback
# provenance, the bounded history). Its schema and semantics belong to the platform
# (`src/core/foundation-installation`), and its location is resolved by the deployment-path authority.
#
# It is deliberately NOT version controlled: it records what IS running rather than what the owner
# authors, so committing it would turn every health evaluation and rejected candidate into a source
# change, and would let a machine's working tree stop matching the immutable revision it is running.
# Durability comes from the deployment's own filesystem, and a Foundation release never carries it.
#
# Establishment (`pnpm installation:establish`, `scripts/installation/README.md`) writes it ONCE, as the
# last act of creating an installation — which is why a target without it is visibly incomplete — and
# refuses a seed whose capsule does not carry this rule.
operational-state.json
